{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":1767179,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,30]],"date-time":"2026-09-30T23:22:34Z","timestamp":1790810554630,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"SCITEPRESS - Science and Technology Publications","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022]]},"DOI":"10.5220\/0011327500003283","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,14]],"date-time":"2022-07-14T20:19:10Z","timestamp":1657829950000},"page":"406-414","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["zkBeacon: Proven Randomness Beacon based on Zero-knowledge Verifiable Computation"],"prefix":"10.5220","author":[{"given":"Thomas","family":"Lavaur","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"ISAE-Supaero, Universit\u00e9 de Toulouse, France, --- Select a Country ---"},{"name":"Paul Sabatier, Universit\u00e9 de Toulouse, France, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"J\u00e9r\u00f4me","family":"Lacan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"ISAE-Supaero, Universit\u00e9 de Toulouse, France, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"3171","event":{"name":"19th International Conference on Security and Cryptography","location":"Lisbon, Portugal","start":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,11]]},"end":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,13]]}},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 19th International Conference on Security and Cryptography"],"original-title":["zkBeacon: Proven Randomness Beacon based on Zero-knowledge Verifiable Computation"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,28]],"date-time":"2022-07-28T08:22:28Z","timestamp":1658996548000},"score":38.9213,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.scitepress.org\/DigitalLibrary\/Link.aspx?doi=10.5220\/0011327500003283"}},"subtitle":[""],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0011327500003283","published":{"date-parts":[[2022]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,21]],"date-time":"2026-08-21T00:27:55Z","timestamp":1787272075720,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Sekolah Tinggi Informatika dan Komputer Indonesia","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IC-ITECHS"],"abstract":"<jats:p>In order to eliminate the reliance on centralized authoritiesthe MA-CPABE ciphertext access control scheme based onblockchain technology has become acurrent researchhotspot, However, the existing solutions still face challengesin terms of blockchain scalability and verifiable security.Therefore, this paper proposes a verifable key calculationscheme based on zero-knowledge proof, aiming to achieve aneffcient and verifiable new type of MA-CPABE access controlscheme. Firstly, during the process of generating the user'sprivate key on the blockchain node, computationally intensiveoperations such as public and private key calculation, hashcalculation, and point addition are performed off-chain,achieving the functions of key generation and distributionSecondly, with the aid of the non-interactive zero-knowledgeproof system, the correctness of the off-chain calculationresults is efficiently verified on-chain to ensure the reliabilityand transparency of the key generation process. Finally, thispaper conducts a comprehensive analysis of the scheme fromthree aspects: security, off-chain computing efficiency, andon-chain cost, The simulation experiment results show thatthe scheme proposed in this paper can achieve trusted keygeneration and distribution in MA-CPABE, reduce the onchain computing overhead,and ensure theexecutionefficiency of the CPABE scheme. It provides a new solution forblockchain-based ciphertext access control.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.32664\/m89bx941","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,21]],"date-time":"2026-08-21T00:08:08Z","timestamp":1787270888000},"page":"560-567","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Verifiable Key Computation Scheme Based on Zero-Knowledge Proof in MA-CPABE"],"prefix":"10.32664","volume":"6","author":[{"family":"Xie Long","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"17895","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,20]]},"container-title":["IC-ITECHS"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.ubhinus.ac.id\/IC-ITECHS\/article\/download\/2554\/1296","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.ubhinus.ac.id\/IC-ITECHS\/article\/download\/2554\/1296","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,21]],"date-time":"2026-08-21T00:08:08Z","timestamp":1787270888000},"score":31.601244,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/jurnal.ubhinus.ac.id\/IC-ITECHS\/article\/view\/2554"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,20]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,24]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.32664\/m89bx941","ISSN":["2580-7234","2356-4407"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2580-7234","type":"electronic"},{"value":"2356-4407","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,20]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,25]],"date-time":"2026-08-25T15:30:50Z","timestamp":1787671850416,"version":"build-2736575974"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"group-title":"SSRN","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Elsevier BV","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]],"date-time":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1767225600000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<jats:p>Retiring a stateful agent is not the same as deleting a model. A deployed agent accretes a durable, multi-dimensional attack surface (cached credentials and OAuth tokens, tool and Model Context Protocol (MCP) bindings, persistent memory, learned policy state, and agent-to-agent (A2A) trust relationships), any component of which, if left behind, becomes a latent foothold for a zombie or ghost agent. Existing techniques address these dimensions in isolation: machine unlearning erases parametric memory, credential schemes bound token lifetimes, and secure-deletion protocols sanitise storage, but no approach jointly retires all five dimensions or, critically, proves that it has done so to a party that does not trust the operator. We present EPITAPH, a unified decommissioning protocol that (i) formalises an agent's disposable state and an accompanying completeness predicate, (ii) coordinates severance, cryptographic erasure, and revocation across all five dimensions, and (iii) emits an operator-independent, transparency-logged Proofof-Decommissioning (PoD) that any auditor can verify. We give a machine-checked formal model: a TLA + safety\/liveness specification of the distributed teardown and a Tamarin symbolic analysis of the attestation protocol under a Dolev-Yao adversary with a compromised operator. A simulation over 50,000 heterogeneous retirements shows that EPITAPH contains all five dimensions for 99.4% of agents within a median of 9.5 s (p99 405 s), holds residual-access probability to 0.4%, and reduces postdecommission resurrection to 0.01% under stated hardwaretrust and peer-expiry assumptions; revocation-only (C,T) and unlearning-only strategies, by contrast, leave 88.7% and 98.2% residual exposure. EPITAPH operationalises the secure end-of-life requirements of emerging security standards for agentic systems.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7341378","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,25]],"date-time":"2026-08-25T14:53:11Z","timestamp":1787669591000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["EPITAPH: Verifiable Decommissioning of Stateful Agentic Systems"],"prefix":"10.2139","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7067-7848","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Mohamed Chahine","family":"Ghanem","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"78","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,25]],"date-time":"2026-08-25T14:53:11Z","timestamp":1787669591000},"score":29.815899,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.ssrn.com\/abstract=7341378"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7341378","published":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,21]],"date-time":"2026-10-21T18:40:02Z","timestamp":1792608002262,"version":"4.5.0"},"publisher-location":"New York, NY, USA","reference-count":42,"publisher":"ACM","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,11,7]],"date-time":"2022-11-07T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1667779200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.acm.org\/publications\/policies\/copyright_policy#Background"}],"funder":[{"name":"Ministerio de Ciencia e Innovaci\u00f3n, Spain","award":["RTI2018-102043-B-I00,EUR2019-103816,RED2018-102321-T"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["RTI2018-102043-B-I00,EUR2019-103816,RED2018-102321-T"]}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000781","name":"European Research Council","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["101001283"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["101001283"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000781","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"name":"Comunidad de Madrid","award":["S2018\/TCS-4339"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["S2018\/TCS-4339"]}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["dl.acm.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,11,7]]},"DOI":"10.1145\/3548606.3560630","type":"proceedings-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,11,7]],"date-time":"2022-11-07T11:41:28Z","timestamp":1667821288000},"page":"1067-1080","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["Efficient Zero-Knowledge Proofs on Signed Data with Applications to Verifiable Computation on Data Streams"],"prefix":"10.1145","author":[{"given":"Dario","family":"Fiore","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"IMDEA Software Institute, Madrid, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ida","family":"Tucker","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"IMDEA Software Institute, Madrid, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"320","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2022,11,7]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_3_2_1_1_1","volume-title":"Homomorphic Network Coding Signatures in the Standard Model. In PKC 2011 (LNCS","volume":"34","author":"Attrapadung Nuttapong","year":"2011","unstructured":"Nuttapong Attrapadung and Beno\u00eet Libert . 2011 . Homomorphic Network Coding Signatures in the Standard Model. In PKC 2011 (LNCS , Vol. 6571),, Dario Catalano, Nelly Fazio, Rosario Gennaro, and Antonio Nicolosi (Eds.). Springer, Heidelberg, Germany, Taormina, Italy, 17-- 34 . https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-642-19379-8_2 10.1007\/978-3-642-19379-8_2 Nuttapong Attrapadung and Beno\u00eet Libert. 2011. Homomorphic Network Coding Signatures in the Standard Model. In PKC 2011 (LNCS, Vol. 6571),, Dario Catalano, Nelly Fazio, Rosario Gennaro, and Antonio Nicolosi (Eds.). Springer, Heidelberg, Germany, Taormina, Italy, 17--34. https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-642-19379-8_2"},{"key":"e_1_3_2_1_2_1","volume-title":"Computing on Authenticated Data: New Privacy Definitions and Constructions. In ASIACRYPT 2012 (LNCS","volume":"385","author":"Attrapadung Nuttapong","year":"2012","unstructured":"Nuttapong Attrapadung , Beno\u00eet Libert , and Thomas Peters . 2012 . Computing on Authenticated Data: New Privacy Definitions and Constructions. In ASIACRYPT 2012 (LNCS , Vol. 7658),, Xiaoyun Wang and Kazue Sako (Eds.). Springer, Heidel